---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Projects — Chike Okonta" activeNav="projects">
  <header class="topbar container">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow">Projects</div>
      <strong class="topbar-title">Technical work in more detail</strong>
    </div>
  </header>
  <main class="section container page-gap">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <span class="section-tag">Selected work</span>
      <h1 class="page-title">Projects</h1>
      <p>Case-study style summaries for systems, tools, and experiments with technical depth.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="panel project-card project-card--featured">
        <div class="project-topline">Research · March 2026</div>
        <h3>DAN: Dynamic Agent Network</h3>
        <p>
          A distributed architecture for orchestrating adaptive multi-agent AI systems at scale.
          Separates global coordination (stateless router with bandit-based planner selection) from
          local learning (case-based Q-learning with non-parametric episodic memory), enabling
          horizontal scaling and fault isolation across distributed server pods.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Global router + specialized local planners</li>
          <li>Case-based Q-learning with Boltzmann retrieval</li>
          <li>A2A ↔ MCP protocol bridging layer</li>
          <li>Optimized for small models at the edge</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="publication-strip publication-strip--project">
          <span class="publication-pill">Published research</span>
          <span class="publication-pill">DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.19041902</span>
        </div>
        <div class="project-links">
          <a href="/posts/dan-dynamic-agent-network">Read overview →</a>
          <a href="https://zenodo.org/records/19041902" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Published paper ↗</a>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="panel project-card">
        <div class="project-topline">AI / orchestration</div>
        <h3>Autopilot systems</h3>
        <p>
          Persistent task handling, event-driven execution, agent coordination, and operational
          memory for systems that need to do more than answer prompts.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Workflow state</li>
          <li>Task routing</li>
          <li>Human-in-the-loop boundaries</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article class="panel project-card">
        <div class="project-topline">Developer tools</div>
        <h3>Node + local runtime experiments</h3>
        <p>
          Execution environments, node-based capability models, and practical operator experiences
          for tool-using systems.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Local-first execution</li>
          <li>CLI/API integration</li>
          <li>Operator UX</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article class="panel project-card">
        <div class="project-topline">Systems thinking</div>
        <h3>Technical product architecture</h3>
        <p>
          Notes and prototypes around control planes, execution planes, and the difference between
          novelty and durable leverage.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Architecture notes</li>
          <li>Platform tradeoffs</li>
          <li>Engineering strategy</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
